      "title": "Solving a Bernoulli Differential Equation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "31d69c14-3d43-5861-b974-708473b62931",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+2 \\cdot \\left(x+5\\right) \\cdot y=\\left(x+5\\right) \\cdot y^{2}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $\\left(x+5\\right)>0$. Choose constants and intervals on which the displayed expressions are real and finite.\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "This is a Bernoulli equation with\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}p(x)&=2 \\cdot \\left(x+5\\right)\\\\ q(x)&=\\left(x+5\\right)\\\\ n&=2.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivide by $y^{2}$ and set $z=y^{-1}$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{y^{2}}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$$\n\nHence the linear equation in standard form is\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(- 2 \\cdot \\left(x+5\\right)\\right)z=- \\left(x+5\\right).$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$I(x)=e^{\\int - 2 \\cdot \\left(x+5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{- \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}.$$\n\nMultiplying through and using the product rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(e^{- \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}\\,z\\right)=- \\left(x+5\\right) \\cdot e^{- \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}.$$\n\nIntegrating with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$e^{- \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}z=\\frac{e^{- \\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}}{2}+C.$$\n\nThus\n\n$$z=C \\cdot e^{\\left(x+5\\right)^{2}} + \\frac{1}{2}.$$\n\nFinally, substitute $z=y^{-1}$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$y=\\frac{2}{2 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{\\left(x+5\\right)^{2}} + 1}.$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant; exclude singularities and restrict to the stated real intervals.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "1733064e-2af1-5c13-8150-0f64d0a7f936",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "0440f07d-7abc-5be7-a7b0-9db3ba0cd136",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\frac{1}{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{\\left(x+5\\right)^{2}}{2}} - 1}"
            },
            {
