  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186147454,
      "id": "17061f4e-da7c-58f9-90b4-47bdc21505da",
      "title": "Solving a Bernoulli Differential Equation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1d3f24cb-97da-5da3-8aba-e7c64368cd6f",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}- \\left(x+2\\right)^{2} \\cdot y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}}{y^{4}}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $\\left(x+2\\right)>0$. Choose constants and intervals on which the displayed expressions are real and finite.\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "This is a Bernoulli equation with\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}p(x)&=- \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\\\\ q(x)&=- 3 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\\\\ n&=-4.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivide by $y^{-4}$ and set $z=y^{5}$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}=5 \\cdot y^{4}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$$\n\nHence the linear equation in standard form is\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(- 5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\\right)z=- 15 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}.$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$I(x)=e^{\\int - 5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{- \\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}}.$$\n\nMultiplying through and using the product rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}}\\,z\\right)=- 15 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2} \\cdot e^{- \\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}}.$$\n\nIntegrating with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$e^{- \\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}}z=3 \\cdot e^{- \\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}}+C.$$\n\nThus\n\n$$z=C \\cdot e^{\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} + 3.$$\n\nFinally, substitute $z=y^{5}$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$y=\\sqrt[5]{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} + 3}.$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant; exclude singularities and restrict to the stated real intervals.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "f5b11735-285f-50d0-bafb-aa1c07ed639d",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "338ff4f0-3a11-5a8f-9018-bd3b65986134",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\sqrt[5]{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{10 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} - 1}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "ae46f471-4864-57b2-b7b7-848e8cfc74a2",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\sqrt[5]{C \\cdot e^{\\frac{10 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{3}}{3}} + \\frac{1}{2}}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8c3b2d85-5b75-5c99-9d5d-4373bdefcbd4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
