  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186147454,
      "id": "17061f4e-da7c-58f9-90b4-47bdc21505da",
      "title": "Solving a Bernoulli Differential Equation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8d37cd9a-c509-5116-b909-ec6ed6581fc9",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}- y=2 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}.\n$$ Take $y>0$. For even powers and powers of $2/3$ in the choices, retain only intervals where the base is positive. Choose constants and intervals on which the displayed expressions are real and finite.\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "This is a Bernoulli equation with\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}p(x)&=-1\\\\ q(x)&=2\\\\ n&=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivide by $y^{\\frac{1}{2}}$ and set $z=y^{\\frac{1}{2}}$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2 \\cdot \\sqrt{y}}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$$\n\nHence the linear equation in standard form is\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)z=1.$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$I(x)=e^{\\int - \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}.$$\n\nMultiplying through and using the product rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\,z\\right)=e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}.$$\n\nIntegrating with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}z=- 2 \\cdot e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}+C.$$\n\nThus\n\n$$z=C \\cdot e^{\\frac{x}{2}} - 2.$$\n\nFinally, substitute $z=y^{\\frac{1}{2}}$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{x}{2}} - 2\\right)^{2}.$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant; exclude singularities and restrict to the stated real intervals. The displayed expression for $z$ must be positive because $z=y^{\\frac{1}{2}}>0$.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "3aa2a280-658c-5ed4-b3df-a4940ed56ade",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "965bce7f-7d53-5604-8a87-b8deb318b0bd",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{3 \\cdot x}{2}} + \\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "b3969ff2-6d3c-58e4-8c89-d92a1101d208",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{x}{2}} + 3\\right)^{2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "b9a16bd0-0920-519c-b26c-ded9fc5a18bd",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{x}{2}} - 2\\right)^{2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "d3bcaed3-855d-58b7-a25d-d2790375f9d5",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{x}{2}} - 1\\right)^{2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "5adbe860-2f8f-562d-94e9-9eeec9be1f43",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{3 \\cdot x}{2}} + \\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{2}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "b9a16bd0-0920-519c-b26c-ded9fc5a18bd"
