  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186147454,
      "id": "17061f4e-da7c-58f9-90b4-47bdc21505da",
      "title": "Solving a Bernoulli Differential Equation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "093d1b6c-952f-5053-81d9-a9d7411a9698",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}- \\frac{y}{\\left(x+3\\right)}=- \\sqrt{\\left(x+3\\right)} \\cdot y^{2}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $\\left(x+3\\right)>0$. Choose constants and intervals on which the displayed expressions are real and finite.\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "This is a Bernoulli equation with\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}p(x)&=- \\frac{1}{\\left(x+3\\right)}\\\\ q(x)&=- \\sqrt{\\left(x+3\\right)}\\\\ n&=2.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivide by $y^{2}$ and set $z=y^{-1}$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{y^{2}}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$$\n\nHence the linear equation in standard form is\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(\\frac{1}{\\left(x+3\\right)}\\right)z=\\sqrt{\\left(x+3\\right)}.$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$I(x)=e^{\\int \\frac{1}{\\left(x+3\\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=\\left(x+3\\right).$$\n\nMultiplying through and using the product rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\left(x+3\\right)\\,z\\right)=\\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}.$$\n\nIntegrating with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\\left(x+3\\right)z=\\frac{2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{5}+C.$$\n\nThus\n\n$$z=\\frac{C}{\\left(x+3\\right)} + \\frac{2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{5}.$$\n\nFinally, substitute $z=y^{-1}$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$y=\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)}{5 \\cdot C + 2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}.$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant; exclude singularities and restrict to the stated real intervals.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "896b218f-a707-5706-ba57-82aee2498380",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "ea4b1ff7-79e0-5db6-a971-6e3ca4450dd4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\frac{9 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{3}}{9 \\cdot C - 2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{9}{2}}}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "3a279116-44b1-5440-97b5-158854c6e1ef",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\frac{5 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)}{5 \\cdot C + 2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "6cadbc52-5912-53c5-965f-98cdac4e4695",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\frac{7 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{2}}{7 \\cdot C + 4 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e59e5cce-cfa6-525b-a511-5ca1b860e962",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\frac{9 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{3}}{9 \\cdot C + 2 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{9}{2}}}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "7991ccf7-f9b7-51ac-814d-7b7d48f05650",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\frac{7 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{2}}{7 \\cdot C - 6 \\cdot \\left(x+3\\right)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
