  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186147454,
      "id": "17061f4e-da7c-58f9-90b4-47bdc21505da",
      "title": "Solving a Bernoulli Differential Equation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "54f0a96d-c485-512e-8cf1-6c6c6ce46c7f",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+3 \\cdot y=3 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) \\cdot y^{3}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $\\left(x-3\\right)>0$. Choose constants and intervals on which the displayed expressions are real and finite.\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "This is a Bernoulli equation with\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}p(x)&=3\\\\ q(x)&=3 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)\\\\ n&=3.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivide by $y^{3}$ and set $z=y^{-2}$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{2}{y^{3}}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$$\n\nHence the linear equation in standard form is\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(-6\\right)z=- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right).$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$I(x)=e^{\\int -6\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)}.$$\n\nMultiplying through and using the product rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(e^{- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)}\\,z\\right)=- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) \\cdot e^{- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)}.$$\n\nIntegrating with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$e^{- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)}z=\\left(\\left(x-3\\right) + \\frac{1}{6}\\right) \\cdot e^{- 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)}+C.$$\n\nThus\n\n$$z=C \\cdot e^{6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + \\left(x-3\\right) + \\frac{1}{6}.$$\n\nFinally, substitute $z=y^{-2}$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$y=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{6}{6 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + 6 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) + 1}}.$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary real constant; exclude singularities and restrict to the stated real intervals. Both signs are retained wherever the radicand is positive.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "478f235f-54aa-51fa-aeda-8a30102e6489",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "d4b2dc8c-2b34-5889-bbcd-1e751fb64fd1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "y=\\pm\\sqrt{- \\frac{4}{- 4 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{4 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + 4 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) + 1}}"
            },
            {
